---
title: "2 · Create a case template"
description: Create a blank case template in the department workspace and open it in the template editor.
sidebar:
  order: 3
  label: "2 · Create a case template"
---

**Who:** tenant admin, or a user with **Template access**. **Where:** the department workspace › **Cases** › **Templates**.

In this example the template is called `Sample Client Onboarding` and has four sections.

## The empty Cases board

Select **Cases** in the sidebar. A workspace without case types shows **No case types in this workspace yet**. Select **Create case template** to go to the template list.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/cases-empty" caption="The Cases board of a workspace without case types." /%}

## Open Templates

You can also open the template list from the sidebar: select the small arrow next to **Cases** to expand it, and then select **Templates**.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/templates-open" caption="Cases expanded in the sidebar, with Templates below it." /%}

## The template list

A new workspace has no templates yet.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/templates-empty" caption="The template list of a new workspace." /%}

## Create a blank template

{% steps %}

1. Select **New blank template**. The **New case type** form opens on the page.
2. In **Name**, enter the template name, for example `Sample Client Onboarding`. In a department workspace you do not choose the department: it is set by this workspace. In a cross-department workspace, choose it in **Department**.
3. Select **Create**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/template-new" caption="The New case type form." /%}

## The editor opens

A new template starts with one section, `Checklist`, that holds one task, `First step`. Rename them, and then add more sections and tasks.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/editor-new" caption="The template editor of a new template." /%}
